    "A profile is a named set of hosts entries. Select one in the sidebar and click Apply to make it active — the active profile is marked with a checkmark. The System Default profile holds your original hosts file; apply it to restore your machine to how it was before Hosts Switchr.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A profile is a named set of hosts entries. Select one in the sidebar and click Apply to make it active — the active profile is marked with a checkmark. The System Default profile holds your original hosts file; apply it to restore your machine to how it was before Hosts Switchr."
          }
        },
        "en-GB": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A profile is a named set of hosts entries. Select one in the sidebar and click Apply to make it active — the active profile is marked with a checkmark. The System Default profile holds your original hosts file; apply it to restore your machine to how it was before Hosts Switchr."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Un perfil es un conjunto de entradas hosts con nombre. Selecciona uno en la barra lateral y haz clic en Aplicar para activarlo; el perfil activo se indica con una marca de verificación. El perfil System Default contiene tu archivo hosts original: aplícalo para dejar el Mac como estaba antes de Hosts Switchr."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Un profil est un ensemble nommé d’entrées hosts. Sélectionnez-en un dans la barre latérale et cliquez sur Appliquer pour l’activer ; le profil actif est signalé par une coche. Le profil System Default contient votre fichier hosts d’origine : appliquez-le pour remettre votre Mac dans l’état où il était avant Hosts Switchr."
          }
        }
      }
    },
