    "Apply merges your content in order — local profile entries, then enabled fragments, then source lists — and writes the result to /etc/hosts. macOS asks for your administrator password because that file is system-owned. Your previous hosts file is backed up automatically before each apply.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Apply merges your content in order — local profile entries, then enabled fragments, then source lists — and writes the result to /etc/hosts. macOS asks for your administrator password because that file is system-owned. Your previous hosts file is backed up automatically before each apply."
          }
        },
        "en-GB": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Apply merges your content in order — local profile entries, then enabled fragments, then source lists — and writes the result to /etc/hosts. macOS asks for your administrator password because that file is system-owned. Your previous hosts file is backed up automatically before each apply."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Aplicar combina tu contenido en orden (entradas locales del perfil, luego los fragmentos activados y después las listas de fuentes) y escribe el resultado en /etc/hosts. macOS pide tu contraseña de administrador porque ese archivo pertenece al sistema. Se hace una copia de seguridad de tu archivo hosts anterior antes de cada aplicación."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Appliquer fusionne votre contenu dans l’ordre — entrées locales du profil, puis fragments activés, puis listes des sources — et écrit le résultat dans /etc/hosts. macOS demande votre mot de passe administrateur car ce fichier appartient au système. Votre fichier hosts précédent est sauvegardé automatiquement avant chaque application."
          }
        }
      }
    },
