    "Fragments are reusable snippets you toggle on per profile, such as a \"Docker\" or \"Staging\" block. Enabled fragments are merged into the active profile under a \"# <name>\" header so you can see where they came from.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fragments are reusable snippets you toggle on per profile, such as a \"Docker\" or \"Staging\" block. Enabled fragments are merged into the active profile under a \"# <name>\" header so you can see where they came from."
          }
        },
        "en-GB": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fragments are reusable snippets you toggle on per profile, such as a \"Docker\" or \"Staging\" block. Enabled fragments are merged into the active profile under a \"# <name>\" header so you can see where they came from."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Los fragmentos son bloques reutilizables que activas en cada perfil, como uno de «Docker» o «Staging». Los fragmentos activados se combinan en el perfil activo bajo una cabecera «# <nombre>», para que veas de dónde vienen."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Les fragments sont des extraits réutilisables que vous activez profil par profil, par exemple un bloc « Docker » ou « Staging ». Les fragments activés sont fusionnés dans le profil actif sous un en-tête « # <nom> », ce qui permet de voir d’où ils viennent."
          }
        }
      }
    },
